{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fltxn4yrkk7hmjzk5fmxw4o2nnnvkimvc23tepj2br57lsukrqfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C.\n\n## Result\n\n**No divergences found.** The pre-existing translation of `c_src/src/lib.c` is correct; I made no changes to `src/lib.rs` (only added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]`).\n\n## Phase artifacts (`translation/`)\n\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | All 10 C symbols; `nm -D` diff is **empty**, 0 missing, 0 stubs |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 34 rejection rows — the C's *entire* error surface is the three `default: return 0;` arms of `collided`; no asserts, null checks, or range checks exist anywhere |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 66 valid-input rows, all checked |\n\n## Tests — 93 total, all passing\n\nAll calls go through `libloading` into **both** `.so`s; every float is compared by `to_bits()` so NaN payloads and signed-zero are part of the assertion.\n\n- `phase_b_vector.rs` (25) — `c2V`/`Minv`/`Maxv`/`Clampv`/`Dot`/`Sub`\n- `phase_b_collision.rs` (30) — the three collision routines + `collided` dispatch, incl. unaligned buffers, aliasing, tag/pointee mismatch\n- `phase_c_errors.rs` (35) — one per `ERRORS.md` row, plus tags `0..=4096` exhaustively and NULL/dangling pointers on reject paths\n- `phase_d_symbols.rs` (3) — automated `nm -D` parity gate\n\nCoverage: ~1.4M randomized cases (fixed-seed splitmix64), plus exhaustive small cross-products (all 255 NaN subsets for `c2AABBtoAABB`, the full 3⁸ ±inf/0 grid).\n\n## Test sensitivity proven (5 negative controls)\n\nRather than trust green results, I mutated the Rust and confirmed detection:\n\n| Mutation | Detected by |\n|---|---|\n| `f32::min/max` instead of C's non-suppressing ternary | 8 tests |\n| Plain `a.x*b.x + a.y*b.y` instead of operand-ordered `mulss`/`addss` | 2 tests |\n| Removed the AABB-vs-circle **argument swap** (lib.c:88) | 3 tests |\n| `<` → `<=` boundary flips | 15 tests |\n| Unknown enum tag falling through instead of returning `0` | 2 failures + SIGSEGV |\n\nNotably, the `mulss`/`addss` NaN-ordering machinery and the argument swap are both genuinely load-bearing — removing either diverges from C.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **No driver binary** in either tree (no `add_executable`, no `[[bin]]`/`src/main.rs`), so the stdout-comparison gate is not applicable.\n- **No `[features]` table** ⇒ the only combinations are default and `--no-default-features`. `run_all.sh` verifies both × both cargo profiles (4 configs) and re-checks the symbol diff; it auto-enumerates a feature power set if features are ever added.\n- One harness fix was needed: `cargo test` doesn't build `cdylib` artifacts, so the debug `.so` was absent — the harness now builds it on demand.\n- Ground truth is the C at **`-O0`** (CMakeLists sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`). At `-O2` gcc reassociates `c2Dot`, changing which NaN payload survives when multiple *distinct* NaN payloads are passed; that affects only multi-distinct-NaN inputs, and the existing `src/lib.rs` doc comment already documents this.\n\nRun everything with `cd translation && bash run_all.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":118343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":261,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4262ae2-0f4e-4595-b6d5-edb6e23770da","uuid":"42c5de53-5302-4ea7-aa8d-0dce3482fdd7","timestamp":"2026-09-04T23:54:01.337Z"}
